     <details class="pyntacle-details nested">
     <summary>mesoscale<span class="chev"></span></summary>
     <div class="pyntacle-details-body">

  Metrics: · Generalized Topological Overlap Measure (GTOM): A measure of neighborhood similarity between all pairs of nodes in a graph. GTOM assigns a value in the range [0,1], this occurs when the neighborhoods of two nodes are identical or one is a subset of the other. · Topological Importance (TI): TI of a node measures its influence in a network through k-step structural propagation. It is computed as the row sum of the k-th power of the edge effect matrix, capturing indirect interactions up to path length k. · Weighted Topological Importance (WI): similar to TI it measures a node's influence in a network by accounting for both the strength and reach of its interactions. · Species Topological Overlap (STO): quantifies pairwise structural similarity based on shared 1-step effects, extended to kk-step propagation. A threshold θθ is applied to filter out weak overlaps.

  :doc:`Open mesoscale </cli/mesoscale/index>`

  .. raw:: html

     </div>
     </details>

  .. raw:: html

     <details class="pyntacle-details nested">
     <summary>percolation<span class="chev"></span></summary>
     <div class="pyntacle-details-body">

  Percolation dynamics: · Local edge thresholds p_th,ij: for each edge (i,j) a local threshold p_th,ij is drawn in [0, p_thMax] from the chosen distribution. · Global percolation probability P*: controls how many edges become "open". An edge (i,j) can transmit only if P* ≥ p_th,ij → A*_ij = 1, otherwise A*_ij = 0. · Spreading from a seed node: starting from the seed s at t = 0, activity spreads along open edges. The active set evolves as S_{t+1} = N_open(S_t) \ R_t, where N_open(S_t) are neighbors reachable through open edges and R_t are recovered nodes. · Recovery time τ: a node activated at time t stays active for τ steps and then recovers (it no longer transmits).

  :doc:`Open percolation </cli/percolation/index>`

  .. raw:: html

     </div>
     </details>

